-- title:
--   Uniformiser and integral basis of a local quaternion division algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, and write $H=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_p,(a),(b)]$ for the quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ with $i^2=a$, $j^2=b$ generated by the images of $a,b$. Assume: every nonzero element of $H$ is a unit (so $H$ is a division algebra); $t,n\in\mathbb{Z}$ are such that $x^2-tx+n\neq 0$ for every $x\in\mathbb{Z}/p$, i.e. the polynomial $X^2-tX+n$ has no root modulo $p$; every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}_p$ is of the form $c^2+tcd+nd^2$ with $c,d\in\mathbb{Z}_p$; and $\theta\in H$ satisfies $\theta^2-t\theta+n=0$. Then there exists $\varpi\in H$ with $\varpi^2=p$ and $\varpi\theta=(t-\theta)\varpi$, such that $\operatorname{trd}\theta:=2\theta_{\mathrm{re}}=t$ and $\operatorname{nrd}\theta:=\theta_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\theta_{i}^2-b\theta_{j}^2+ab\,\theta_{k}^2=n$, while $\operatorname{trd}\varpi=0$ and $\operatorname{trd}(\theta\varpi)=0$; moreover $1,\theta,\varpi,\theta\varpi$ are linearly independent over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (any $c_0,c_1,c_2,c_3\in\mathbb{Q}_p$ with $c_0+c_1\theta+c_2\varpi+c_3\theta\varpi=0$ all vanish), and for every $m\in H$ one has $\|\operatorname{nrd} m\|\le 1$ if and only if $m=c_0+c_1\theta+c_2\varpi+c_3\theta\varpi$ for some $c_0,c_1,c_2,c_3\in\mathbb{Z}_p$.
--
--   This is the standard structure theorem for the unique quaternion division algebra over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, presented as a cyclic algebra over the unramified quadratic subfield $\mathbb{Q}_p(\theta)$ with uniformiser $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi^2=p$ and $\varpi\theta=\bar\theta\varpi$, together with the identification of its unique maximal order, the set of elements of reduced norm of absolute value at most $1$, as the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-span of $1,\theta,\varpi,\theta\varpi$. It is used in the construction of coordinates on maximal orders in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOrderCoord_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOrderCoord_of_isMaximalOrder).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_exists_sq_eq_natCast_and_setOf_norm_nrd_le_one_eq_of_forall_isUnit_padic.lean

